{"source":"github","project_id":"webfakes","target":"r-lib/webfakes","id":"pr/87","ref":87,"title":"Restrict overmatching MACH ifdef to only trigger on OSX and Mach","description":"Hurd also uses Mach.\r\nhttps://www.gnu.org/software/hurd/hurd/porting/guidelines.html\r\n```\r\n#ifdef __MACH__\r\nSome applications put Apple Darwin-specific code inside #ifdef __MACH__ guards. Such guard is clearly not enough, since not only Apple uses Mach as a kernel. This should be replaced by #if defined(__MACH__) \u0026\u0026 defined(__APPLE__)\r\n```\r\n\r\nCloses #86.","published_at":"2022-09-24T00:32:47Z","updated_at":"2023-02-08T11:00:29Z","url":"https://github.com/r-lib/webfakes/pull/87","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"Zopolis4","merged_at":"2023-02-08T11:00:29Z","state":"MERGED"}}
